        "updated_at": "2026-11-05T01:51:58Z",
        "body": "Update on the local check-rules-safety run: I stopped it after 2 h 55 min at full CPU, unfinished. It was re-running every one of the 538 rules touched by #779 and this PR against the benign corpora, and several of those rules are slow on long inputs (the ReDoS baseline lists some), so it never got through.\n\nFor this PR the gate cannot show anything new. Only `compliance.nist_ai_rmf` changed; the engine never reads `compliance`; and parsing all 511 files before and after shows every other field, detection included, is identical. So every rule matches exactly what it matches on main.\n\nWhen this PR retargets to main, validate.yml will run the same gate in CI and may hit the same wall. A follow-up worth doing: have check-rules-safety skip rules whose detection, agent_source and test cases are unchanged from the base.\n"
